import Definitions.Accounting.Headline.Sm120

/-!
# sm_120's measured headline instance: VF3r-16 and H1 + fx1 (trusted; generated)

Written by `benchmarks/pouw/lean_headline.py` from the machine model's data (`benchmarks/pouw/machine_model/data`), and
checked against it by `benchmarks/pouw/tests/test_lean_headline.py`: edit the data and rerun the exporter, never this
file. `Accounting.Guarantees.TS.Sm120MeasuredHeadline` reads it.

* `rowNames`, `vf3r16`, `machine`: the measured vector VF3r-16, 109 rows of SMSP-cycles a warp
  instruction at its epoch's census, each sparse over `Sm120.classes`; every facet SM-clocked, f_max 2430 MHz.
* `h1fx1`, `model`: H1 + fx1 (`dither-c-peel-fx1`) on that machine. Its writer kinds are the census's MMA forms, each at
  the committed words an instruction of it writes (forms.toml: `m·n·k_dense/(L·split)` at L = 32,
  rounded up), and the uniform `UNI` (1); `MMA` (the forms' fallback line) and `UNI64` (VF3r-16 prices it on the
  uniform pipe alone) are not on the menu. `Sm120.h1fx1`'s vector classes, fold routes and `N_w`; SCALAR-ROUTE's
  floors `q = q_T = 9/8`, `b_T = 0`.
* `flatSkip`, `flat`: ♭ is `Sm120.flat`'s word production and fold, with ε_skip's skippable work at VF3r-16's
  0.362755% (`eps_budget.design_skip` on VF3r-16), at NOROW's price on π*.
* `piStar`, `wStarKind`: π*, the facet (JI3s_0) the machine model's LP certificate sits on at
  q* = 9/8, and the writer kind (honest's IMMA16832) that is the cheapest word route there.
-/

